attempt, I stumbled upon an expensive wand in a shop on dlvl 5.  Zzzzap, a
wish: 2 blessed scrolls of charging.  I already had a pair of speed boots,
so I got fixed +3 GoP, +3 SDSM, +3 HoB, blessed Magic Marker, and, since I
didn't have the money for the wand, a blessed figurine of an Archon.

The Archon turned out to be the key to the speed ascension, clearing out the
shopkeeper and sweeping monsters out of my path level after level.  The wand
was actually (0:3), and I soon burned the final wish from the wand on a
magic whistle.  I quickly descended, fighting the almost irrepressible urge
to explore, and I found some bones on dlvl 13 with CoMR, a sack with some
holy water, and assorted other gear.

I cancelled scrolls and potions, wrote some ?ID, ?MM, and ?EA, then the
Archon and I cleared the castle and the first wish from that /oWishing (also
(0:3)) went for a Bag of Holding, which I needed badly at that point.  I
then dug down quickly to dlvl 50, marked the VS, wished for a =oTC, drank a
!oConfusion, and levelported to the quest level.

I zapped the quest nemesis with a /oDeath, grabbed the bell, double
levelported down to find Vlad's.  Quickly getting the candleabrum, I
returned to hell, zapped /oDigging down, down to find Rodney and his book.
I the big room in Rodney's castle a purple worm ate my Archon - NOOOOOOOO!
Ah well, I had her for 5000 turns and she'd fulfilled her purpose of getting
me most of the way there very quickly.

Zapped a /oDeath at the Wizard of Yendor, grabbed the Book of the Dead,
levelported once again to the bottom of hell, and performed the ritual at
turn 6400 or so, dealing again with the wizard at that juncture.  I then
used another wish for unholy water to curse a !GL and a ?oTeleport, went
down to the Sactum, immediately back up, then levelported back down to end
up in the inner sanctum, near the altar-room.  I used conflict and found my
